import QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceTwoTerm
import QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking

/-!
# A crossing-covariant, strand-labelled QED insertion on the 3-strand Hecke representation

Front: owner-authorised option 4 (2026-11-20), "a crossing-covariant, non-pairwise QED operator
and a derived scale `c_em`". Companion to `NucleonWeightSpaceTwoTerm` (fixed-position charge
operators) and to the sibling branch's `NucleonQEDCovariance` (commutant of `{A₁, A₂}`), and to
`BorromeanPairwiseLinking` / `MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus` (the combinatorial linking data on the
corpus's Borromean word `(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³`).

## The construction

A braid word is read letter by letter while the **component labels** of the strands are carried
along (`BorromeanPairwiseLinking.swapAt` / `finalPerm`). At a letter that exchanges the strands
labelled `a, b`, the generator `σ` is deformed to first order

    σ  ↦  σ · (1 + ε · Y_{ab}),     σ⁻¹ ↦ (1 − ε · Y_{ab}) · σ⁻¹,

so the two-letter cancellation `σ σ⁻¹ = 1` holds to first order automatically. The insertion is
**local**: `Y_{ab}` lies in the subalgebra generated by that one crossing, `span{1, σ}`, with
label-dependent coefficients, `Y_{ab} = α_{ab} • 1 + β_{ab} • σ`. A QED insertion has
`α_{ab}, β_{ab} ∝ Q_a Q_b`.

## What is proved

* **§A — covariance forces a scalar.** The first-order defect of the braid relation
  `σ₁σ₂σ₁ = σ₂σ₁σ₂` is exactly `β_{ac} • (σ₁² − σ₂²)`, where `{a, c}` is the pair exchanged by the
  *middle* letter (`r3Defect_eq`). On the `(2,1)` weight space `σ₁² − σ₂²` has `(0,0)` entry
  `q² − 1`, so for `q² ≠ 1` covariance is equivalent to `β_{ac} = 0` (`r3Defect_eq_zero_iff`).
  Every pair is the middle pair of some labelling, so **all `β` vanish**
  (`beta_eq_zero_of_covariant`): the only crossing-covariant local insertion is a **scalar**.
* **§B — the fixed-position charge insertion is not covariant.** Using the position operators
  `Q₁₂, Q₂₃` (which do commute with their own crossing) as `Y` gives a first-order defect with
  `(2,2)` entry `−(2/3)(q − q⁻¹)(q² + 1)` (`posDefect_22`), nonzero for `q⁴ ≠ 1`. On the weight space the
  flavour does **not** travel with the strand at `q ≠ 1`, because `Ř` is not the permutation.
* **§C — the scalar insertion is a colored writhe.** With a scalar `Y`, the deformed word is the
  undeformed word times a scalar factor (`defWord_eq_smul`), whose first-order coefficient is the
  label-weighted signed crossing count `colWrithe` (`fac_first_order`). That count is invariant
  under the two-letter cancellation and the braid relation, for every starting labelling
  (`colWrithe_r2_*`, `colWrithe_r3_*`); and it decomposes as `Σ_{pairs} α_{st} · crossSum s t`
  (`colWrithe_eq_pairs`), i.e. `Σ α_{st} · 2 lk_{st}` on a pure braid.
* **On `V³ = (σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³` the first-order variation is identically zero at every `q`**
  (`borromean_firstOrder_trace_zero`): all three pairwise crossing sums vanish
  (`BorromeanPairwiseLinking.borromean_crossSum_zero`), so the colored writhe is `0` for every
  label coefficient `α` — in particular for proton charges `(2/3, 2/3, −1/3)` and neutron charges
  `(2/3, −1/3, −1/3)`. The `n − p` splitting from this operator is `0`, not merely at `q = 1`.
* **§C′ — the full crossing commutant.** Allowing the insertion to range over the whole
  commutant of its crossing (5-dim) adds, by exact computation at `q = 2`, only the global
  commutant element `Z`; such an insertion contributes `colWrithe · Z · w` at first order
  (`facZ_first_order`, `defWordZ_eq`) and so also vanishes on `V³`
  (`borromean_firstOrder_traceZ_zero`). The classification is measured at one `q`; the
  vanishing theorem holds for every `Z` commuting with the generators.
* **§D — the three-body linear term.** A coupling of an *alternating* invariant (the Milnor
  `μ̄₁₂₃` reverses sign under an odd relabelling; `MilnorTripleLinkingMagnus.mubar_swap_eq_neg`)
  that is covariant under relabelling needs a charge coefficient alternating under the same
  exchange; any such coefficient vanishes when the two exchanged charges are equal
  (`alternating_coeff_vanishes_on_equal_charges`), which is the case for both nucleons
  (two `u`, resp. two `d`). The *even* coupling `c₃ · Q₁Q₂Q₃ · μ̄²` survives, and its `n − p`
  value is `(2/9) · c₃ · μ̄²` (`evenThreeBody_np_split`) — **with `c₃` not derived here**.

## Scope (AGENTS.md (a)/(b))

§A is a structural exclusion **within the stated class** (first-order, local insertions in
`span{1, σ}` with label-dependent coefficients), the invariant being the braid relation itself.
It is not a statement about nonlocal or higher-order insertions. §C's zero is exact for that
class. §D's linear prune is structural; the even branch is **open** (its coefficient `c₃` is not
derived), and it is not fitted here.

-- Ref: [kassel1995] (Hecke representation of the braid group; braid relations);
-- [milnor1957] (`μ̄` invariants; antisymmetry under odd relabelling).
-/

namespace QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CrossingCovariantQED

open Matrix
open QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceTraces
open QOU.BraidsAndKnots.NucleonWeightSpaceTwoTerm
open QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanPairwiseLinking

variable {R : Type*} [Field R]

/-! ## §A. A local, label-dependent first-order insertion is covariant only if it is scalar -/

/-- The `(2,1)`-weight-space generators with `h = q − q⁻¹` left as an independent symbol, so
that identities can be proved by polynomial arithmetic and specialised afterwards. -/
def G₁ {S : Type*} [CommRing S] (h q : S) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) S := !![q, 0, 0; 0, 0, 1; 0, 1, h]

/-- See `G₁`. -/
def G₂ {S : Type*} [CommRing S] (h q : S) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) S := !![0, 1, 0; 1, h, 0; 0, 0, q]

theorem A₁_eq_G₁ (q : R) : A₁ q = G₁ (q - q⁻¹) q := rfl
theorem A₂_eq_G₂ (q : R) : A₂ q = G₂ (q - q⁻¹) q := rfl

/-- The local insertion over a commutative ring. -/
def localInsG {S : Type*} [CommRing S] (a b : S) (X : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) S) :
    Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) S := a • (1 : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) S) + b • X

/-- First-order defect of `σ₁σ₂σ₁ = σ₂σ₁σ₂` under the deformation `σ ↦ σ(1 + εY)`, with the
strands initially labelled `(a, b, c)`. Left side: `σ₁` exchanges `{a,b}`, `σ₂` exchanges
`{a,c}`, `σ₁` exchanges `{b,c}`. Right side: `σ₂` exchanges `{b,c}`, `σ₁` exchanges `{a,c}`,
`σ₂` exchanges `{a,b}`. Generic commutative ring `S` (§7c). -/
def r3DefectG {S : Type*} [CommRing S] (h q aab bab aac bac abc bbc : S) :
    Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) S :=
  (G₁ h q * localInsG aab bab (G₁ h q) * G₂ h q * G₁ h q
    + G₁ h q * G₂ h q * localInsG aac bac (G₂ h q) * G₁ h q
    + G₁ h q * G₂ h q * G₁ h q * localInsG abc bbc (G₁ h q))
  - (G₂ h q * localInsG abc bbc (G₂ h q) * G₁ h q * G₂ h q
    + G₂ h q * G₁ h q * localInsG aac bac (G₁ h q) * G₂ h q
    + G₂ h q * G₁ h q * G₂ h q * localInsG aab bab (G₂ h q))

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000 in
/-- **The defect is carried entirely by the middle pair's `σ`-coefficient**, given the Hecke
parameter relation `h·q = q² − 1` (i.e. `h = q − q⁻¹`). -/
theorem r3DefectG_eq {S : Type*} [CommRing S] (h q aab bab aac bac abc bbc : S)
    (hh : h * q - q ^ 2 + 1 = 0) :
    r3DefectG h q aab bab aac bac abc bbc
      = bac • (G₁ h q * G₂ h q * G₂ h q * G₁ h q - G₂ h q * G₁ h q * G₁ h q * G₂ h q) := by
  have e1 : localInsG aab bab (G₁ h q) = !![aab + bab * q, 0, 0; 0, aab, bab; 0, bab, aab + bab * h] := by
    ext i j; fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [localInsG, G₁]
  have e2 : localInsG aac bac (G₂ h q) = !![aac, bac, 0; bac, aac + bac * h, 0; 0, 0, aac + bac * q] := by
    ext i j; fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [localInsG, G₂]
  have e3 : localInsG abc bbc (G₁ h q) = !![abc + bbc * q, 0, 0; 0, abc, bbc; 0, bbc, abc + bbc * h] := by
    ext i j; fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [localInsG, G₁]
  have e4 : localInsG abc bbc (G₂ h q) = !![abc, bbc, 0; bbc, abc + bbc * h, 0; 0, 0, abc + bbc * q] := by
    ext i j; fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [localInsG, G₂]
  have e5 : localInsG aac bac (G₁ h q) = !![aac + bac * q, 0, 0; 0, aac, bac; 0, bac, aac + bac * h] := by
    ext i j; fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [localInsG, G₁]
  have e6 : localInsG aab bab (G₂ h q) = !![aab, bab, 0; bab, aab + bab * h, 0; 0, 0, aab + bab * q] := by
    ext i j; fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;> simp [localInsG, G₂]
  rw [r3DefectG, e1, e2, e3, e4, e5, e6]
  ext i j
  fin_cases i <;> fin_cases j <;>
    simp [G₁, G₂, Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three] <;>
    first
    | ring1
    | linear_combination (bab * h) * hh
    | linear_combination (bbc * h) * hh
    | linear_combination (h * (aab + aac + abc + bab * h + bab * q + bbc * h + bbc * q)) * hh

theorem mid_diff_00 {S : Type*} [CommRing S] (h q : S) :
    (G₁ h q * G₂ h q * G₂ h q * G₁ h q - G₂ h q * G₁ h q * G₁ h q * G₂ h q) 0 0 = q ^ 2 - 1 := by
  simp [G₁, G₂, Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three]; ring

/-- The defect on the actual `(2,1)` weight-space generators. -/
def r3Defect (q aab bab aac bac abc bbc : R) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R :=
  r3DefectG (q - q⁻¹) q aab bab aac bac abc bbc

theorem r3Defect_eq (q aab bab aac bac abc bbc : R) (hq : q ≠ 0) :
    r3Defect q aab bab aac bac abc bbc
      = bac • (A₁ q * A₂ q * A₂ q * A₁ q - A₂ q * A₁ q * A₁ q * A₂ q) := by
  rw [r3Defect, r3DefectG_eq _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ (by field_simp; ring)]; rfl

/-- The `(0,0)` entry of `σ₁σ₂²σ₁ − σ₂σ₁²σ₂` on the `(2,1)` weight space. -/
theorem sq_diff_00 (q : R) :
    (A₁ q * A₂ q * A₂ q * A₁ q - A₂ q * A₁ q * A₁ q * A₂ q) 0 0 = q ^ 2 - 1 :=
  mid_diff_00 (q - q⁻¹) q

/-- **Covariance ⇔ the middle pair's `σ`-coefficient vanishes** (for `q² ≠ 1`). -/
theorem r3Defect_eq_zero_iff (q aab bab aac bac abc bbc : R) (hq : q ≠ 0) (hq2 : q ^ 2 ≠ 1) :
    r3Defect q aab bab aac bac abc bbc = 0 ↔ bac = 0 := by
  rw [r3Defect_eq q aab bab aac bac abc bbc hq]
  constructor
  · intro h
    have h00 := congrFun (congrFun h 0) 0
    rw [Matrix.smul_apply, sq_diff_00] at h00
    simp only [Matrix.zero_apply, smul_eq_mul] at h00
    rcases mul_eq_zero.mp h00 with h1 | h1
    · exact h1
    · exact absurd (sub_eq_zero.mp h1) hq2
  · intro h; rw [h, zero_smul]

/-- **Every pair is the middle pair of some labelling, so covariance kills every `β`.**
`α β : Fin 3 → Fin 3 → R` are the label-dependent coefficients (symmetric in the pair).
Hypothesis: the braid relation holds to first order for **every** labelling `(a, b, c)` of the
three strands by distinct components. Conclusion: `β x y = 0` for all distinct `x, y`. -/
theorem beta_eq_zero_of_covariant (q : R) (hq : q ≠ 0) (hq2 : q ^ 2 ≠ 1)
    (α β : Fin 3 → Fin 3 → R)
    (hcov : ∀ a b c : Fin 3, a ≠ b → a ≠ c → b ≠ c →
      r3Defect q (α a b) (β a b) (α a c) (β a c) (α b c) (β b c) = 0)
    (x y : Fin 3) (hxy : x ≠ y) : β x y = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨z, hzx, hzy⟩ : ∃ z : Fin 3, z ≠ x ∧ z ≠ y := by
    fin_cases x <;> fin_cases y <;> simp_all <;> decide
  exact (r3Defect_eq_zero_iff q _ _ _ _ _ _ hq hq2).mp
    (hcov x z y (Ne.symm hzx) hxy (hzy))

/-- **Negative control**: the scalar (`β = 0`) insertion is covariant for every `α`. -/
theorem r3Defect_scalar (q aab aac abc : R) (hq : q ≠ 0) :
    r3Defect q aab 0 aac 0 abc 0 = 0 := by
  rw [r3Defect_eq q aab 0 aac 0 abc 0 hq, zero_smul]

/-- **And the obstruction is real**: a nonzero middle coefficient breaks covariance. -/
theorem r3Defect_ne_zero (q aab bab bac abc bbc aac : R) (hq : q ≠ 0) (hq2 : q ^ 2 ≠ 1)
    (hb : bac ≠ 0) : r3Defect q aab bab aac bac abc bbc ≠ 0 := fun h =>
  hb ((r3Defect_eq_zero_iff q aab bab aac bac abc bbc hq hq2).mp h)

/-! ## §B. The fixed-position charge insertion is not covariant -/

/-- First-order braid-relation defect when the insertion at a `σ₁` letter is the position
operator `Q₁₂` and at a `σ₂` letter is `Q₂₃` (proton weight space). -/
def posDefect (q : R) : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R :=
  (A₁ q * Q12p * A₂ q * A₁ q + A₁ q * A₂ q * Q23p * A₁ q + A₁ q * A₂ q * A₁ q * Q12p)
  - (A₂ q * Q23p * A₁ q * A₂ q + A₂ q * A₁ q * Q12p * A₂ q + A₂ q * A₁ q * A₂ q * Q23p)

theorem posDefect_22 (q : R) (hq : q ≠ 0) (h3 : (3 : R) ≠ 0) :
    posDefect q 2 2 = -(2 / 3) * (q - q⁻¹) * (q ^ 2 + 1) := by
  simp only [posDefect, A₁, A₂, Q12p, Q23p, Matrix.sub_apply, Matrix.add_apply,
    Matrix.mul_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three]
  simp
  have h9 : (9 : R) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [show (9 : R) = 3 * 3 by norm_num]; exact mul_ne_zero h3 h3
  field_simp
  ring

theorem posDefect_ne_zero (q : R) (hq : q ≠ 0) (h2 : (2 : R) ≠ 0) (h3 : (3 : R) ≠ 0)
    (hq2 : q ^ 2 ≠ 1) (hq2' : q ^ 2 + 1 ≠ 0) : posDefect q ≠ 0 := by
  intro h
  have h22 := congrFun (congrFun h 2) 2
  rw [posDefect_22 q hq h3, Matrix.zero_apply] at h22
  have hh : q - q⁻¹ ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    apply hq2
    have : q * (q - q⁻¹) = q ^ 2 - 1 := by field_simp
    rw [h0, mul_zero] at this
    linear_combination -this
  have h23 : (2 / 3 : R) ≠ 0 := div_ne_zero h2 h3
  exact mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero (neg_ne_zero.mpr h23) hh) hq2' h22

/-! ## §C. The scalar insertion is a colored writhe, and it vanishes on `V³` -/

/-- A braid letter evaluated on the proton weight space. Letter `(0, ·)` is `σ₁`, `(1, ·)` is
`σ₂`; sign `1` is the generator, any other sign its inverse. -/
def gen (q : R) : Letter → Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R
  | (i, e) => if i = 0 then (if e = 1 then A₁ q else A₁Inv q)
              else (if e = 1 then A₂ q else A₂Inv q)

/-- The undeformed word. -/
def wordL (q : R) : List Letter → Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R
  | [] => 1
  | l :: w => gen q l * wordL q w

/-- The label pair `(a, b)` exchanged by letter `i` at labelling `pos`. -/
def pairAt (pos : List ℕ) (i : ℕ) : ℕ × ℕ := (pos.getD i 0, pos.getD (i + 1) 0)

/-- The word deformed by the **scalar** label-dependent insertion
`σ^e ↦ (1 + ε·e·α_{ab}) σ^e`. -/
def defWord (q ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) : List Letter → List ℕ → Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R
  | [], _ => 1
  | (i, e) :: w, pos =>
      ((1 : R) + ε * (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2) • gen q (i, e)
        * defWord q ε α w (swapAt pos i)

/-- The scalar factor accumulated along the word. -/
def fac (ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) : List Letter → List ℕ → R
  | [], _ => 1
  | (i, e) :: w, pos =>
      ((1 : R) + ε * (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2)
        * fac ε α w (swapAt pos i)

/-- The **colored writhe**: label-weighted signed crossing count. -/
def colWrithe (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) : List Letter → List ℕ → R
  | [], _ => 0
  | (i, e) :: w, pos =>
      (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2 + colWrithe α w (swapAt pos i)

theorem defWord_eq_smul (q ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (w : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    defWord q ε α w pos = fac ε α w pos • wordL q w := by
  induction w generalizing pos with
  | nil => simp [defWord, fac, wordL]
  | cons l w ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    simp only [defWord, fac, wordL, ih, Matrix.smul_mul, Matrix.mul_smul, smul_smul, mul_comm]

/-- **First-order coefficient of the scalar deformation is the colored writhe.** -/
theorem fac_first_order (ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (w : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    ∃ r : R, fac ε α w pos = 1 + ε * colWrithe α w pos + ε ^ 2 * r := by
  induction w generalizing pos with
  | nil => exact ⟨0, by simp [fac, colWrithe]⟩
  | cons l w ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := ih (swapAt pos i)
    refine ⟨(e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2 * colWrithe α w (swapAt pos i)
        + r + ε * ((e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2) * r, ?_⟩
    simp only [fac, colWrithe, hr]; ring

/-- The trace of the deformed word: `(1 + ε·colWrithe + O(ε²)) · tr(w)`. -/
theorem trace_defWord_first_order (q ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (w : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    ∃ r : R, trace (defWord q ε α w pos)
      = trace (wordL q w) + ε * colWrithe α w pos * trace (wordL q w)
        + ε ^ 2 * r * trace (wordL q w) := by
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := fac_first_order ε α w pos
  refine ⟨r, ?_⟩
  rw [defWord_eq_smul, Matrix.trace_smul, hr, smul_eq_mul]; ring

/-! ### Covariance of the colored writhe -/

theorem colWrithe_append (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (u v : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    colWrithe α (u ++ v) pos = colWrithe α u pos + colWrithe α v (finalPerm u pos) := by
  induction u generalizing pos with
  | nil => simp [colWrithe, finalPerm]
  | cons l u ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    simp only [List.cons_append, colWrithe, finalPerm, ih]; ring

theorem finalPerm_append (u v : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    finalPerm (u ++ v) pos = finalPerm v (finalPerm u pos) := by
  induction u generalizing pos with
  | nil => rfl
  | cons l u ih => obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l; simp [finalPerm, ih]

/-- The six labellings of three strands by components `0, 1, 2`. -/
def perms3 : List (List ℕ) := [[0,1,2],[0,2,1],[1,0,2],[1,2,0],[2,0,1],[2,1,0]]

/-- `pairAt` of the R3/R2 local words, tabulated: the local moves exchange the same label pairs
with the same signs on both sides. This is the only finite check the covariance needs. -/
theorem r3_pairs (e : ℤ) : ∀ p ∈ perms3,
    finalPerm [(0, e), (1, e), (0, e)] p = finalPerm [(1, e), (0, e), (1, e)] p ∧
    pairAt p 0 = pairAt (swapAt (swapAt p 1) 0) 1 ∧
    pairAt (swapAt p 0) 1 = pairAt (swapAt p 1) 0 ∧
    pairAt (swapAt (swapAt p 0) 1) 0 = pairAt p 1 := by
  intro p hp
  simp only [perms3, List.mem_cons, List.mem_nil_iff, or_false] at hp
  rcases hp with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl <;> simp only [finalPerm] <;> decide

/-- `colWrithe` sees an unordered pair: it is enough that `α` be symmetric. -/
theorem colWrithe_r3 (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (e : ℤ) (p : List ℕ) (hp : p ∈ perms3) :
    colWrithe α [(0, e), (1, e), (0, e)] p = colWrithe α [(1, e), (0, e), (1, e)] p := by
  obtain ⟨_, h1, h2, h3⟩ := r3_pairs e p hp
  simp only [colWrithe]
  rw [h1, h2, h3]; ring

theorem colWrithe_r2 (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (hα : ∀ a b, α a b = α b a) (i : ℕ) (e : ℤ)
    (p : List ℕ) (hi : i ≤ 1) (hp : p ∈ perms3) :
    colWrithe α [(i, e), (i, -e)] p = 0 := by
  have key : pairAt (swapAt p i) i = ((pairAt p i).2, (pairAt p i).1) := by
    simp only [perms3, List.mem_cons, List.mem_nil_iff, or_false] at hp
    interval_cases i <;> rcases hp with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl <;> decide
  simp only [colWrithe, key, hα (pairAt p i).2 (pairAt p i).1]
  push_cast; ring

/-- **Covariance in context**: replacing an R3 left side by its right side anywhere in a word
(whose prefix keeps the labelling a permutation, e.g. any word in `σ₁^{±1}, σ₂^{±1}`) does not
change the colored writhe. -/
theorem colWrithe_r3_context (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (e : ℤ) (u v : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ)
    (hu : finalPerm u pos ∈ perms3) :
    colWrithe α (u ++ [(0, e), (1, e), (0, e)] ++ v) pos
      = colWrithe α (u ++ [(1, e), (0, e), (1, e)] ++ v) pos := by
  obtain ⟨hf, -⟩ := r3_pairs e _ hu
  simp only [List.append_assoc, colWrithe_append, finalPerm_append, hf,
    colWrithe_r3 α e _ hu]

theorem colWrithe_r2_context (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (hα : ∀ a b, α a b = α b a) (i : ℕ) (e : ℤ)
    (hi : i ≤ 1) (u v : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) (hu : finalPerm u pos ∈ perms3) :
    colWrithe α (u ++ [(i, e), (i, -e)] ++ v) pos = colWrithe α (u ++ v) pos := by
  have hfp : finalPerm [(i, e), (i, -e)] (finalPerm u pos) = finalPerm u pos := by
    have hp := hu
    simp only [perms3, List.mem_cons, List.mem_nil_iff, or_false] at hp
    simp only [finalPerm]
    interval_cases i <;> rcases hp with h | h | h | h | h | h <;> rw [h] <;> decide
  simp only [List.append_assoc, colWrithe_append, finalPerm_append, hfp,
    colWrithe_r2 α hα i e _ hi hu, zero_add]

/-- Single swaps keep a labelling a permutation. -/
theorem swapAt_mem_perms3 (p : List ℕ) (i : ℕ) (hp : p ∈ perms3) (hi : i ≤ 1) :
    swapAt p i ∈ perms3 := by
  simp only [perms3, List.mem_cons, List.mem_nil_iff, or_false] at hp
  interval_cases i <;> rcases hp with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl <;> decide

/-- Any word in `σ₁^{±1}, σ₂^{±1}` keeps a labelling a permutation. -/
theorem finalPerm_mem_perms3 (w : List Letter) (hw : ∀ l ∈ w, l.1 ≤ 1) (p : List ℕ)
    (hp : p ∈ perms3) : finalPerm w p ∈ perms3 := by
  induction w generalizing p with
  | nil => exact hp
  | cons l w ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    exact ih (fun l hl => hw l (List.mem_cons_of_mem _ hl)) _
      (swapAt_mem_perms3 p i hp (hw (i, e) List.mem_cons_self))

/-! ### The colored writhe is the linking-number energy, and it vanishes on `V³` -/

/-- One letter's contribution, rewritten as a sum over the three unordered label pairs. -/
theorem letter_eq_pairs (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (hα : ∀ a b, α a b = α b a) (p : List ℕ)
    (hp : p ∈ perms3) (i : ℕ) (hi : i ≤ 1) (e : ℤ) :
    (e : R) * α (pairAt p i).1 (pairAt p i).2
      = α 0 1 * ((crossSum 0 1 [(i, e)] p : ℤ) : R)
        + α 0 2 * ((crossSum 0 2 [(i, e)] p : ℤ) : R)
        + α 1 2 * ((crossSum 1 2 [(i, e)] p : ℤ) : R) := by
  simp only [perms3, List.mem_cons, List.mem_nil_iff, or_false] at hp
  interval_cases i <;> rcases hp with rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl | rfl <;>
    simp [pairAt, crossSum, swapAt, hα 1 0, hα 2 0, hα 2 1] <;> ring

theorem crossSum_append (s t : ℕ) (u v : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    crossSum s t (u ++ v) pos = crossSum s t u pos + crossSum s t v (finalPerm u pos) := by
  induction u generalizing pos with
  | nil => simp [crossSum, finalPerm]
  | cons l u ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    simp only [List.cons_append, crossSum, finalPerm, ih]; ring

/-- **The scalar first-order QED term reduces to linking numbers**: for any word in
`σ₁^{±1}, σ₂^{±1}` and any symmetric pair coefficient `α`,
`colWrithe = Σ_{s<t} α_{st} · crossSum_{st}` (`crossSum = 2·lk` on a pure braid). -/
theorem colWrithe_eq_pairs (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (hα : ∀ a b, α a b = α b a)
    (w : List Letter) (hw : ∀ l ∈ w, l.1 ≤ 1) (p : List ℕ) (hp : p ∈ perms3) :
    colWrithe α w p = α 0 1 * ((crossSum 0 1 w p : ℤ) : R)
      + α 0 2 * ((crossSum 0 2 w p : ℤ) : R) + α 1 2 * ((crossSum 1 2 w p : ℤ) : R) := by
  induction w generalizing p with
  | nil => simp [colWrithe, crossSum]
  | cons l w ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    have hi : i ≤ 1 := hw (i, e) List.mem_cons_self
    have hw' : ∀ l ∈ w, l.1 ≤ 1 := fun l hl => hw l (List.mem_cons_of_mem _ hl)
    have hsplit : ∀ s t, crossSum s t ((i, e) :: w) p
        = crossSum s t [(i, e)] p + crossSum s t w (swapAt p i) := fun s t => by
      have := crossSum_append s t [(i, e)] w p
      simpa [finalPerm] using this
    simp only [colWrithe]
    rw [ih hw' _ (swapAt_mem_perms3 p i hp hi), letter_eq_pairs α hα p hp i hi e,
      hsplit 0 1, hsplit 0 2, hsplit 1 2]
    push_cast; ring

/-- **The colored writhe vanishes on the Borromean nucleon `V³ = (σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³`, for every
symmetric label coefficient `α`** — hence for proton and neutron charge assignments alike. -/
theorem colWrithe_borromean_zero (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (hα : ∀ a b, α a b = α b a) :
    colWrithe α borWord [0, 1, 2] = 0 := by
  have hb := borromean_crossSum_zero
  simp only [Prod.mk.injEq] at hb
  rw [colWrithe_eq_pairs α hα borWord (by decide) _ (by decide), hb.1, hb.2.1, hb.2.2]
  simp

/-- **Main result.** The first-order variation of the trace of `V³` under the (unique, by §A)
crossing-covariant local insertion is zero, at every `q`: the deformed trace is
`tr(V³) + O(ε²)`. -/
theorem borromean_firstOrder_trace_zero (q ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R)
    (hα : ∀ a b, α a b = α b a) :
    ∃ r : R, trace (defWord q ε α borWord [0, 1, 2])
      = trace (wordL q borWord) + ε ^ 2 * r * trace (wordL q borWord) := by
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := trace_defWord_first_order q ε α borWord [0, 1, 2]
  exact ⟨r, by rw [hr, colWrithe_borromean_zero α hα]; ring⟩

/-- Proton component charges `(u, u, d)` as the label coefficient `Q_a Q_b`. -/
def protonPair (a b : ℕ) : R :=
  (if a = 2 then (-1 / 3 : R) else 2 / 3) * (if b = 2 then (-1 / 3 : R) else 2 / 3)

/-- Neutron component charges `(u, d, d)`. -/
def neutronPair (a b : ℕ) : R :=
  (if a = 0 then (2 / 3 : R) else -1 / 3) * (if b = 0 then (2 / 3 : R) else -1 / 3)

/-- **The `n − p` splitting from this operator is zero at first order, at every `q`.** -/
theorem np_split_firstOrder_zero :
    colWrithe (neutronPair (R := R)) borWord [0, 1, 2]
      - colWrithe (protonPair (R := R)) borWord [0, 1, 2] = 0 := by
  rw [colWrithe_borromean_zero _ (fun a b => by simp [neutronPair, mul_comm]),
    colWrithe_borromean_zero _ (fun a b => by simp [protonPair, mul_comm]), sub_zero]

/-- **Negative control**: the same colored writhe is nonzero on the Hopf link `σ₁²`, so the
`V³` zero is a fact about the Borromean word, not about the construction. -/
theorem colWrithe_hopf_eq : colWrithe (protonPair (R := R)) hopfWord [0, 1, 2]
    = 2 * ((2 / 3) * (2 / 3)) := by
  simp [colWrithe, hopfWord, pairAt, swapAt, protonPair]; ring

theorem colWrithe_hopf_ne_zero (h3 : (3 : R) ≠ 0) (h2 : (2 : R) ≠ 0) :
    colWrithe (protonPair (R := R)) hopfWord [0, 1, 2] ≠ 0 := by
  rw [colWrithe_hopf_eq]
  have h23 : (2 / 3 : R) ≠ 0 := div_ne_zero h2 h3
  exact mul_ne_zero h2 (mul_ne_zero h23 h23)

/-! ### Extension: insertions in the global commutant also factor out

Measured (exact rational arithmetic at `q = 2`, `crossing_commutant_covariance_probe.py`): if the
insertion at a crossing is allowed to range over the full **commutant of that crossing**
(5-dimensional on the `(2,1)` weight space, not just `span{1, σ}`), the covariant solutions are
exactly `span{1, Z}` per label pair, `Z` the non-scalar element commuting with **both**
generators (the sibling's `NucleonQEDCovariance.M`). The theorem below shows such an insertion
still contributes `colWrithe · Z · w` at first order, hence zero on `V³`. -/

/-- Accumulated factor for an insertion `σ^e ↦ σ^e (1 + ε·e·α_{ab}·Z)`. -/
def facZ (ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (Z : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R) :
    List Letter → List ℕ → Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R
  | [], _ => 1
  | (i, e) :: w, pos =>
      (1 + (ε * (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2) • Z) * facZ ε α Z w (swapAt pos i)

/-- The word deformed by a `Z`-valued insertion. -/
def defWordZ (q ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (Z : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R) :
    List Letter → List ℕ → Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R
  | [], _ => 1
  | (i, e) :: w, pos =>
      gen q (i, e) * (1 + (ε * (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2) • Z)
        * defWordZ q ε α Z w (swapAt pos i)

theorem facZ_comm (ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (Z X : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R)
    (hZ : Z * X = X * Z) (w : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    facZ ε α Z w pos * X = X * facZ ε α Z w pos := by
  induction w generalizing pos with
  | nil => simp [facZ]
  | cons l w ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    simp only [facZ]
    rw [mul_assoc, ih, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc]
    congr 1
    rw [add_mul, mul_add, one_mul, mul_one, smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, hZ]

theorem defWordZ_eq (q ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (Z : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R)
    (hZ : ∀ l, Z * gen q l = gen q l * Z) (w : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    defWordZ q ε α Z w pos = facZ ε α Z w pos * wordL q w := by
  induction w generalizing pos with
  | nil => simp [defWordZ, facZ, wordL]
  | cons l w ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    simp only [defWordZ, facZ, wordL, ih]
    have h1 : gen q (i, e) * (1 + (ε * (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2) • Z)
        = (1 + (ε * (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2) • Z) * gen q (i, e) := by
      rw [add_mul, mul_add, one_mul, mul_one, smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, hZ]
    have h2 := facZ_comm ε α Z (gen q (i, e)) (hZ (i, e)) w (swapAt pos i)
    rw [h1, mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc (gen q (i, e)), ← h2]
    simp only [mul_assoc]

theorem facZ_first_order (ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (Z : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R)
    (w : List Letter) (pos : List ℕ) :
    ∃ Rm : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R,
      facZ ε α Z w pos = 1 + (ε * colWrithe α w pos) • Z + ε ^ 2 • Rm := by
  induction w generalizing pos with
  | nil => exact ⟨0, by simp [facZ, colWrithe]⟩
  | cons l w ih =>
    obtain ⟨i, e⟩ := l
    obtain ⟨Rm, hRm⟩ := ih (swapAt pos i)
    set x := (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2
    refine ⟨(x * colWrithe α w (swapAt pos i)) • (Z * Z) + Rm + (ε * x) • (Z * Rm), ?_⟩
    have hx : ε * (e : R) * α (pairAt pos i).1 (pairAt pos i).2 = ε * x := by
      simp only [x]; ring
    simp only [facZ, colWrithe, hRm, hx]
    simp only [mul_add, add_mul, one_mul, mul_one, smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, smul_smul,
      smul_add]
    module

/-- **A global-commutant insertion is also first-order trivial on `V³`.** -/
theorem borromean_firstOrder_traceZ_zero (q ε : R) (α : ℕ → ℕ → R) (hα : ∀ a b, α a b = α b a)
    (Z : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R) (hZ : ∀ l, Z * gen q l = gen q l * Z) :
    ∃ Rm : Matrix (Fin 3) (Fin 3) R, trace (defWordZ q ε α Z borWord [0, 1, 2])
      = trace (wordL q borWord) + ε ^ 2 * trace (Rm * wordL q borWord) := by
  obtain ⟨Rm, hRm⟩ := facZ_first_order ε α Z borWord [0, 1, 2]
  refine ⟨Rm, ?_⟩
  rw [defWordZ_eq q ε α Z hZ, hRm, colWrithe_borromean_zero α hα, mul_zero, zero_smul, add_zero,
    add_mul, one_mul, trace_add, smul_mul_assoc, trace_smul, smul_eq_mul]

/-! ## §D. The three-body (Milnor) channel -/

/-- **A charge coefficient alternating under exchange of two strands vanishes when those two
strands carry equal charge** (`2 ≠ 0`). A relabelling-covariant coupling to the alternating
invariant `μ̄₁₂₃` needs such a coefficient; both nucleons have a repeated charge. -/
theorem alternating_coeff_vanishes_on_equal_charges (f : R → R → R → R)
    (halt : ∀ x y z, f x y z = - f y x z) (h2 : (2 : R) ≠ 0) (x z : R) : f x x z = 0 := by
  have h := halt x x z
  have : (2 : R) * f x x z = 0 := by linear_combination h
  rcases mul_eq_zero.mp this with h' | h'
  · exact absurd h' h2
  · exact h'

/-- The symmetric charge monomial on the two nucleons. -/
theorem charge_triple_products (h3 : (3 : R) ≠ 0) :
    ((2 / 3 : R) * (2 / 3) * (-1 / 3) = -4 / 27) ∧ ((2 / 3 : R) * (-1 / 3) * (-1 / 3) = 2 / 27) := by
  have h27 : (27 : R) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [show (27 : R) = 3 * 3 * 3 by norm_num]; exact mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero h3 h3) h3
  constructor <;> field_simp <;> ring

/-- **The surviving even three-body term**: `E₃ = c₃ · Q₁Q₂Q₃ · μ̄²` splits `n − p` by
`(2/9) · c₃ · μ̄²`. `c₃` is a free coefficient here — **not derived** (GAP). -/
theorem evenThreeBody_np_split (h3 : (3 : R) ≠ 0) (c₃ m : R) :
    c₃ * ((2 / 3) * (-1 / 3) * (-1 / 3)) * m ^ 2 - c₃ * ((2 / 3) * (2 / 3) * (-1 / 3)) * m ^ 2
      = (2 / 9) * c₃ * m ^ 2 := by
  have h9 : (9 : R) ≠ 0 := by
    rw [show (9 : R) = 3 * 3 by norm_num]; exact mul_ne_zero h3 h3
  field_simp; ring

end QOU.BraidsAndKnots.CrossingCovariantQED
